<title>JAPAN: Japan auto shares higher, helped by weaker yen.</title>
<headline>Japan auto shares higher, helped by weaker yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in the automobile sector 0#TEQ.T were driven higher in Wednesday morning trade, supported by the yen's weaker trend, traders said.</p>
<p>At 0045 GMT, the share price of Fuji Heavy Industries Ltd was up four yen at 539 yen. Volume was 1.685 million shares, the fifth heaviest in the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Shares of Mazda Motor Corp were up nine yen at 526 yen, on a volume of 839,000 shares.</p>
</text>
